{"schema":1,"id":"birthday-paradox","title":"How many people make a shared birthday likely?","lang":"en","sources":["https://pudding.cool/2018/04/birthday-paradox/","https://mathworld.wolfram.com/BirthdayProblem.html"],"settings":[{"id":"people","label":"People in the room","default":"23","options":[{"value":"10","label":"10"},{"value":"23","label":"23"},{"value":"40","label":"40"}]}],"answer":"A room of 23 people gives a better than even chance that two share a birthday, because 23 people make 253 pairs, each a chance to match","checks":[{"question":"Two separate rooms each hold 23 people. When everyone joins one room, how many new pairs become possible, and why can’t you just add the two rooms’ match probabilities?","answer":"529 new pairs: each of the 23 people in one room can now match each of the 23 in the other. The combined room has 1,035 pairs, compared with 506 within the two separate rooms. Adding the old probabilities misses the cross-room pairs and counts overlapping match events twice."},{"question":"On a planet with 100 equally likely birthdays, would 23 people still be needed for a better than even chance of a shared birthday? Use the person-by-person calculation to find the smallest room.","answer":"No: 13 people suffice. Multiply the chances of avoiding earlier birthdays, 100/100 × 99/100 × … × 88/100, and subtract from 1: about 55.7%. With 12 people it is about 49.7%. A smaller calendar makes each new pair more likely to match."}],"scenarios":[{"values":{"people":"10"},"name":"People in the room: 10","duration":143.7,"paper":"#ffffff","steps":[{"step":"room","title":"Do two of these people share a birthday?","line":"Predict: what is the chance that a room this size holds a shared birthday?","caption":"A year has 365 days, so a match can seem to need a crowd. Each card is one person. Before searching the dates, guess how likely a shared birthday is in a room this size. The chances on this page assume independent birthdays, and give every day of a 365-day year the same chance, with no 29 February.","start":0,"end":21.767,"hold":0.533,"state":{"people":10,"sample":[139,122,300,27,116,316,156,10,140,142],"dates":["19 May","2 May","27 Oct","27 Jan","26 Apr","12 Nov","5 Jun","10 Jan","20 May","22 May"]},"changed":{"people":{"after":10},"sample":{"after":[139,122,300,27,116,316,156,10,140,142]},"dates":{"after":["19 May","2 May","27 Oct","27 Jan","26 Apr","12 Nov","5 Jun","10 Jan","20 May","22 May"]}},"picture":"19 May. 2 May. 27 Oct. 27 Jan. 26 Apr. 12 Nov. 5 Jun. 10 Jan. 20 May. 22 May. 10 people, 10 random birthdays.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│        ┌──────────────┐┌──────────────┐┌─────────────┐┌──────────────┐┌──────────────┐\n│        │    19 May    ││    2 May     ││   27 Oct    ││    27 Jan    ││   26 Apr     │\n│        └──────────────┘└──────────────┘└─────────────┘└──────────────┘└──────────────┘\n│        ┌──────────────┐┌──────────────┐┌─────────────┐┌──────────────┐┌──────────────┐\n│        │    12 Nov    ││    5 Jun     ││   10 Jan    ││    20 May    ││   22 May     │\n│        └──────────────┘└──────────────┘└─────────────┘└──────────────┘└──────────────┘\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│                                10 people, 10 random birthdays\n│\n│"},{"step":"chance","title":"No shared birthday in this room of 10","line":"Is that luck, or usual for a room of 10?","caption":"Most rooms of 10 have no match: of 1,000 random rooms, 112 had a shared birthday, and the exact chance is 11.7%. A room of 23 people gives a better than even chance that two share a birthday, because 23 people make 253 pairs, each a chance to match. The next steps count those pairs.","start":21.767,"end":42.4,"hold":22.467,"state":{"people":10,"shared":[],"chance":0.11694817771107768,"sample":{"seed":137,"trials":1000,"matched":112,"observed":0.112},"days":[139,122,300,27,116,316,156,10,140,142],"dates":["19 May","2 Ma